==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|haust|lang=non}} from earlier {{term|haustr}} (masculine), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*harƀustaz}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*harbistaz}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*kerp-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*skerp-}}. Compare Old English {{term|hærfest|lang=ang}}, English {{term|harvest|lang=en}}, the Old High German {{term|Herbist|lang=goh}}; German {{term|Herbst|lang=de}}, Danish {{term|høst|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|höst|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/høyst/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|øyst|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n}}

# [[autumn]], [[fall]]
#: ''Ég úrskrifaðist '''haustið''' 2007.''
#:: I graduated '''fall''' 2007.

